{"data":[{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2510.23265","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2510.23265","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2510.23265","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"creators":[{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Edmund","familyName":"Karasiewicz","name":"Karasiewicz, Edmund","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Shuichiro","familyName":"Takeda","name":"Takeda, Shuichiro","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Minimal depth $K$-types for wild double covers and Shimura correspondences"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2025,"subjects":[{"subject":"Representation Theory (math.RT)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"Number Theory (math.NT)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Mathematics","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"subject":"11F70, 22E50","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"MSC"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2025-10-27T12:25:05Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025-10-29T00:32:45Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025-11-05T12:33:32Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2025-11-06T01:41:01Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-10-27T13:15:31Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2026-10-28T01:13:12Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2025-10","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"}],"language":null,"types":{"schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint","citeproc":"article","bibtex":"misc","ris":"GEN","resourceType":"Article"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"3","rightsList":[{"rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0"}],"descriptions":[{"descriptionType":"Abstract","description":"Using distinguished pseudo-spherical representations of covering tori constructed in a companion work and Dat's parahoric induction, we construct a distinguished family of representations for an Iwahori subgroup $\\bar{I}$ in $\\bar{G}$, an $n$-fold Brylinski-Deligne (BD) cover of a split connected reductive $p$-adic group $G$, under explicit hypotheses on the BD datum. No tameness assumption $\\mathrm{gcd}(p,n)=1$ is imposed.\n The construction suggests a conjectural theory of Iwahori-types for BD covers beyond the tame case. We verify this for $2$-fold covers of almost simple simply-laced simply-connected Chevalley groups of rank at least $2$ over $2$-adic fields. In particular, for these non-tame $2$-fold covers we prove:\n 1) The pair $(\\bar{I},σ)$ is a Bushnell-Kutzko type for the Bernstein block analogous to the block of unramified principal series in a linear reductive group. This is a non-tame analogue of the Borel-Casselman theorem.\n 2) The Hecke algebra $\\mathcal{H}(\\bar{G},\\bar{I},σ^{\\vee})$ has an Iwahori-Matsumoto presentation up to normalization. In types $A_{r},D_{2r+1},E_{6},E_{7}$ we obtain the complete presentation and show that $\\mathcal{H}(\\bar{G},\\bar{I},σ^{\\vee})$ is isomorphic to the Iwahori-Hecke algebra of an explicit linear group. This determines an equivalence of Bernstein blocks producing a local Shimura correspondence.\n 3) The representation $σ$ extends to a hyperspecial maximal compact subgroup $\\bar{K}$. Among the genuine $\\bar{K}$-representations, $σ$ has minimal depth with respect to the principal congruence filtration. It also yields a finite Shimura correspondence, generalizing a result of Savin."},{"descriptionType":"Other","description":"Revised to incorporate results from arXiv:2608.29548"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.23265","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":3,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"downloadCount":0,"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2025-10-28T03:34:58Z","registered":"2025-10-28T03:34:59Z","published":null,"updated":"2026-10-28T03:14:24Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}}}}],"meta":{"total":1898,"totalPages":1898,"page":1},"links":{"self":"https://api.datacite.org/dois?query=registered%3A%5B2025-10-27T16%3A00%3A00Z+TO+2025-10-28T15%3A59%3A59Z%5D+AND+doi%3A10.48550%2Farxiv.%2A\u0026page%5Bsize%5D=1","next":"https://api.datacite.org/dois?page%5Bnumber%5D=2\u0026page%5Bsize%5D=1\u0026query=registered%3A%5B2025-10-27T16%3A00%3A00Z+TO+2025-10-28T15%3A59%3A59Z%5D+AND+doi%3A10.48550%2Farxiv.%2A"}}